hi my name is Frank Schoenberg and I'm  the Wikimedia Foundation head of public  outreach the Wikimedia Foundation is the  organization behind Wikipedia the  Encyclopedia that everybody can add it  so I'm here today to tell you more about  Wikipedia and why you as a science  student should help Wikipedia to get  better let me start with a story about  what impact Wikipedia can have and this  is the story of Judy and Judy is the  mother of a 20 year old daughter from  Florida and Judy's daughter was  diagnosed with cancer at the age of two  so 18 years ago and at that time  Judy spend hours in medical libraries to  get more information about the specific  type of cancer that her daughter had and  18 years ago I mean she could find  little information about that specific  type of cancer and she couldn't  understand the medical terms she was  reading however her daughter survived  and then 12 years later Judy's daughter  was diagnosed with a different kind of  cancer and this time Judy used the  internet and Wikipedia she was armed  with knowledge about the disease its  causes and possible treatments and she  sent us an email  last year when we were in the middle of  our yearly fundraiser and Judy said  Wikipedia and the Internet has helped me  to gain a sense of control over the  uncontrollable and this is I think this  is a really a nice story to see how  Wikipedia impacts the life of people so  let me  tell you more about Wikipedia let me  give you some numbers and let me tell  you more about who's behind Wikipedia  who writes it let's start with the  numbers Wikipedia right now has 18  million articles in more than 260  languages and what I find really  impressive is that Wikipedia worldwide  all of these language versions get more  than 400 million unique visitors per  month and all the content of Wikipedia  is written by volunteers people like you  and me and there are more than hundred  thousands of volunteers who write  Wikipedia articles and they don't get  paid they just do it because they like  to learn and they like to teach others  and they like to share their knowledge  with others and they all believe in the  same vision that vision statement of the  Wikimedia Foundation that is we believe  that it's good to create a world where  every single human being on this planet  has access to the sum of all knowledge  and now back to the topic so I said I  want to give you some reasons why you  assigned students should help Wikipedia  to get better and I have three reasons  first of all if you write Wikipedia  articles you will learn a lot you will  learn to translate your special  knowledge to a general audience to an  audience of people like Judy who needs  information and who needs information  that is written in an easy-to-understand  language so you will also learn to to  write better you will  improve your writing skills because you  will interact with the community of  Wikipedia editors and the readers and  you will get feedback and people will  tell you hey there is something that I  didn't understand and maybe you can  write it a little bit in a different way  so that feedback is really good and then  also what you will learn is you will  improve your digital media literacy  skills because when you write Wikipedia  articles you will learn a lot about  Wikipedia culture and you will learn a  lot about what makes a good article and  why are some articles not as good as  other articles so you will learn a lot  about how the quality of Wikipedia how  Wikipedia gets created and that's one of  the big learnings so the second reason  why I think you as a science student  should help Wikipedia to get better is  you can give something back so I guess  that most of you use Wikipedia at least  one once a week and let me tell you  about me I use Wikipedia every day and  five years ago I decided I wanted to  give something back to Wikipedia so I  studied history and five years ago I  started to improve history articles on  Wikipedia and that gives me a good  feeling because I'm taking information  from Wikipedia every day I learned a lot  I enjoy reading Wikipedia articles so I  give something back  so the third reason why I think you as a  science student should help Wikipedia to  get better is that huge audience that  Wikipedia has imagined the cancer  article on the English Wikipedia gets  more than 200 and thousand views per  month  isn't that amazing so many views I  remember when I wrote  articles for scientific journals I got  maybe I got 20 years or so but on  Wikipedia my articles get or read much  more people and this is a great thing so  imagine you would help to make the  cancer article better and you would get  more than 200,000 views per month  wouldn't that be great so here's the  three reasons again you will learn a lot  you can give something back to Wikipedia  and you will write for a huge audience  and now there are many ways you can help  Wikipedia to get better you can just  take a look at an article and look at  the language and maybe you want to copy  edit it it's very easy you just click on  the edit button and you can start copy  editing and then you click Save and  everything is done and you've helped  Wikipedia to get better  you can also fact check Wikipedia  articles existing Wikipedia articles or  you can upload pictures or you could  even start a new Wikipedia article and  it's really easy go to Wikipedia click  on the edit button and then start  editing and you can help people like  Judy to find the information that they  need thank you very much  you
 

